  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EU-Ghana Pact for Skills: Integrated Action for Green Jobs and Skills</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;This project represents ILO&#xbf;s contribution to the overall EU-Ghana Pact for Skills, a multiyear Programme bringing together key actors in Ghana&#xbf;s government and civil society with global expertise, aimed at helping Ghana&#xbf;s transition to a smart, green, digitally based economy that will provide decent work for all, particularly those who have been most negatively affected by economic shocks, climate change and exclusion. ILO brings its expertise in demand-driven skills provision, green jobs and gender equality along with its convening power for engaging governments, employers and workers organizations in this work.&amp;nbsp;The ILO will focus on three main issues:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li data-list=&quot;bullet&quot; class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ql-ui&quot; contenteditable=&quot;false&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;The promotion of policy coherence across skills-development programmes and environmental policies&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;to promote green and digital jobs;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li data-list=&quot;bullet&quot; class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ql-ui&quot; contenteditable=&quot;false&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;The reinforcement of national/sectoral constituents&#xbf; and stakeholders&#xbf; capacities to address skills gaps, design and implement skills strategies for green and digital economy&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li data-list=&quot;bullet&quot; class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ql-ui&quot; contenteditable=&quot;false&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;The relevance and accessibility of competency-based TVET programmes that respond to current and future labour market needs.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;It will achieve objectives within the overall scope of the EU-Ghana pact through a diverse set of activities aimed at developing and enhancing the capacity of national actors in policy, skills need identification, skills provision and employment programming.&amp;nbsp;The project builds on and expands the impact of existing and past work by the ILO in these areas in Ghana, and benefits from well established partnerships.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
